@m-wichmann - One thing that I observed in the provided stack trace was that it appears that the exception appears to be on the path of handling a k_timer handler--`rx_timeout()`. That particular k_timer is instantiated by `uart_nrfx_uarte.c`. This could indicate that there may be an alternate method of re-creating the problem on other platforms, or at least other ARM boards by using a periodic timer to call `test_write_irq()`.

Would you be so kind as to attach a copy of your `.config` as well? For reference, this can be found at ...
    `build/zephyr/.config`

I managed to strip away most of my code and got a minimal example that shows the error (error 2). It's more or less like the original code, but the write function is called from a timer. For some reason the problem only shows when I call `uart_rx_enable` on init. There is no UART used in this example except for that call. The problem does not occur every time, but most of the time about 30 to 60 seconds after running this example there is a null pointer in `sys_dlist_remove` that leads to a crash later on.

